<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Real Audiencia of Panama</h1><p class="st-meta">1538 CE – 1751 CE · capital Panamá</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The royal court and government of the Isthmus of Panama, the vital crossing through which Peruvian silver passed on its way to Spain.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/audiencia">Audiencia</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-panama">Panama</a> was established in 1538 to govern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/castilla-de-oro">Castilla de Oro</a> and the surrounding provinces of Tierra Firme. It was briefly abolished in 1543 and restored in the 1560s, and from 1542 it fell within the sphere of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Panama's role was transit: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potosi">Potosí</a> was shipped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-city">Panama City</a>, carried across the isthmus by mule and river, and traded at the great fairs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nombre-de-dios-panama">Nombre de Dios</a> and later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portobelo">Portobelo</a> for European goods. The trade attracted attacks: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-morgan">Henry Morgan</a> sacked <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-panama">Panama</a> City in 1671, and it was rebuilt on a new site in 1673. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-vernon">Edward Vernon</a> captured Portobelo in 1739.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> shifted to sailing around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-horn">Cape Horn</a>, the isthmus declined. The audiencia was abolished in 1751, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-panama">Panama</a> was placed under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viceroyalty-of-new-granada">Viceroyalty of New Granada</a>. It later joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/gran-colombia">Gran Colombia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st